    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50677" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vēsānĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vaesā-</span></b> ),
			īre, 4, v. n.
		vesanus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to be insane</i>, <i>rave</i> (late
			Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dicebat contra deum vesanire Theodosium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Hist. Eccl. 9, 30</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vēsānĭens</span></b> ,
			entis, <i>part.</i>, <i>raging</i>, <i>furious</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vesaniente vento,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					25, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
